module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorLeftUnitorSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.DenominatorQuotients.StalkColonIdeal
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.DenominatorQuotients.Stalks

/-!
# The stalk of the action of the ideal of denominators

Let `X` be a scheme, `L` and `F` sheaves of `𝒪_X`-modules and `s` a meromorphic section of `L`
with ideal of denominators `I`. The first canonical map of
[Stacks, Tag 02P2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02P2) is the inclusion of the product
`I F` in `F`, and that product is *by definition* the image of the canonical action
`η : I ⊗ F ⟶ F`. The stalk of the first denominator quotient `Q₁ = F / I F` of
[Stacks, Tag 02SW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02SW) at a point `x` is therefore the
quotient of `F_x` by the range of the stalk of `η`, which is what
`Stacks.Chow.denominatorQuotientStalkLinearEquiv` says.

This file computes that range: it is the stalk of the ideal of denominators acting on `F_x`,

  `range η_x = (the germs at x of I) · F_x`,

and hence, by the colon-ideal presentation of that stalk, it is
`Ideal.denominatorIdeal a b · F_x` for a local ratio `a / b` of `s` at `x`. That is the shape in
which the length computation of part (4) of Tag 02SW consumes the first quotient: the
coefficient of the cycle `[Q₁]_k` at a point is the length of `F_x / I F_x`, and the length
formula of [Stacks, Tag 02QH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02QH) —
`Ideal.length_fractionalProduct_quotient_sub_length_denominator_quotient` — is stated about
exactly that quotient.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk.denominatorIdealActionStalk` — the stalk at `x` of the canonical
  action `η : I ⊗ F ⟶ F` of Tag 02P2, as a linear map over the local ring.
* `Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk.denominatorQuotientStalkLinearEquivDenominatorIdeal` — the stalk
  of the first denominator quotient as the quotient of `F_x` by `Ideal.denominatorIdeal a b`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk.stalkLinearMap_denominatorIdealAction_germ_tmul` — the stalk of
  the action sends the germ of a local pure tensor `d ⊗ n` to `germ(ι d) • germ(n)`.
* `Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk.range_denominatorIdealActionStalk` — the range of the stalk of
  the action is the ideal generated by the germs of the ideal of denominators, acting on the
  stalk of `F`.
* `Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk.range_denominatorIdealActionStalk_eq_denominatorIdeal_smul` — the
  same range, written with `Ideal.denominatorIdeal` of the germs of a local ratio.
* `Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk.exists_affineOpen_range_denominatorIdealActionStalk_eq` — around
  every point of a scheme there is an affine open carrying a ratio for which that equality holds.
  This is the entry point, and its only hypothesis is that `L` is invertible.

## Implementation notes

Both inclusions pass through local pure tensors, and the two directions use the two halves of the
tensor-stalk comparison `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.tensorStalkIso` of
[Stacks, Tag 01CB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CB) differently. For `range ⊆`, an
element of the stalk of `I ⊗ F` is carried by that comparison to an element of `I_x ⊗ F_x`, which
is a sum of pure tensors of germs; `tensorStalkIso_germ` identifies the preimage of such a tensor
with the germ of a local pure tensor, where the sections-level formula
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.denominatorIdealAction_val_app_toTensorSheafSection` applies. For
`range ⊇`, a germ of a denominator and an element of `F_x` are represented on a common
neighbourhood and recombined into one local pure tensor there; only the sections-level formula is
needed, not the comparison.

The sections-level formula is stated at the `toTensorSheafSection` spelling of the tensor product
of a ringed space, while the stalk map `AlgebraicGeometry.stalkLinearMap` and the quotient
identification of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.DenominatorQuotients.Stalks` are stated at the
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Invertible.tensorProduct` spelling. The two tensor products are
definitionally but not syntactically equal, so the statements here mix them freely but every
bridge between them is applied by `exact` or passed as an argument, never by `rewrite`: at
`implicit` transparency `rewrite` reports that it did not find an occurrence of the pattern.
`AlgebraicGeometry.stalkLinearMap_germ` is the first place this bites, which is why it appears as
the head of a `trans` chain rather than in a `rw`.

`open AlgebraicGeometry hiding denominatorIdeal denominatorIdealι` is required, and is the same
one-line fix that `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.DenominatorQuotients.StalkColonIdeal`
carries: pulling `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.Meromorphic.SectionTransport` into the
import closure — which `AlgebraicGeometry.stalkLinearMap` lives in — makes `denominatorIdeal` and
`denominatorIdealι` ambiguous between `Stacks.DenominatorIdeal`, the spelling this chain uses,
and `AlgebraicGeometry`, whose `denominatorIdealι` carries
[Stacks, Tag 02P1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02P1). The two are genuinely two names
for one object; they are left alone here, and the one place where the proof has to cross between
them — the membership in `Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk.germs`, which is written in the
`Stacks.DenominatorIdeal` spelling — is closed by `rfl`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02SW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02SW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02P2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02P2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02P0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02P0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02QH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02QH)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry hiding denominatorIdeal denominatorIdealι
open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk

variable (X : Scheme.{u}) (L F : X.Modules)
  (s : AlgebraicGeometry.MeromorphicSection X.sheaf L)

/-- The ideal of denominators at the declared type `X.Modules`, written with the
`AlgebraicGeometry` spelling of `denominatorIdeal`. This is **not**
`Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk.denominatorIdealDecl`, which is the same ascription of the
`Stacks.DenominatorIdeal` spelling: the two spellings are two names for one object, and a
statement that mixes them has to unfold both, which exhausts the heartbeat budget of a single
declaration at `whnf`. Everything reached from the sections-level formula for the action is in
the `AlgebraicGeometry` spelling, so that is the one used here. -/
private abbrev denominatorIdealModules : X.Modules := AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s

/-- The stalk at `x` of the canonical action `η : I ⊗ F ⟶ F` of the ideal of denominators of `s`
on `F`, from [Stacks, Tag 02P2], as a linear map over the local ring. Its range is the submodule
of `F_x` divided out by `Stacks.Chow.denominatorQuotientStalkLinearEquiv`. -/
abbrev denominatorIdealActionStalk (x : X) :
    (Stacks.Chow.denominatorIdealTensorModule L F s).presheaf.stalk x →ₗ[X.presheaf.stalk x]
      F.presheaf.stalk x :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.stalkLinearMap (Stacks.Chow.denominatorIdealTensorModule L F s) F
    (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealAction X L F s) x

/-- **The stalk of the action of the ideal of denominators on the germ of a local pure tensor.**
It is the germ of the denominator acting on the germ of the section, by the sections-level formula
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.denominatorIdealAction_val_app_toTensorSheafSection` together with the
compatibility of the action on sections with germs. -/
theorem stalkLinearMap_denominatorIdealAction_germ_tmul (x : X) (U : Opens X) (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (d : (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s).val.obj (op U)) (n : F.val.obj (op U)) :
    denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x
        ((Stacks.Chow.denominatorIdealTensorModule L F s).presheaf.germ U x hxU
          (toTensorSheafSection X.toRingedSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s) F
            (op U) (d ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.obj (op U)] n))) =
      X.presheaf.germ U x hxU
          (((AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op U)).hom d) •
        F.presheaf.germ U x hxU n := by
  refine (AlgebraicGeometry.stalkLinearMap_germ _ F
    (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealAction X L F s) U x hxU _).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (ConcreteCategory.hom (F.presheaf.germ U x hxU))
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.denominatorIdealAction_val_app_toTensorSheafSection X L F s U d n)) ?_
  exact PresheafOfModules.germ_smul (M := F.val) x U hxU _ n

/-- The image of a pure tensor of stalks lies in the germs of the ideal of denominators acting on
the stalk of `F`: representing the two factors on a common neighbourhood exhibits the preimage of
the tensor as the germ of a local pure tensor, by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.tensorStalkIso_germ`. -/
private theorem mem_span_germs_smul_of_tensorStalkIso_symm_tmul (x : X)
    (p : (denominatorIdealModules X L s).presheaf.stalk x) (q : F.presheaf.stalk x) :
    denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x
        ((tensorStalkIso X.toRingedSpace x (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s) F).symm
          (p ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.stalk x] q)) ∈
      Ideal.span (germs X L s x) •
        (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) (F.presheaf.stalk x)) := by
  obtain ⟨W₁, hxW₁, d₁, hd₁⟩ := (denominatorIdealModules X L s).presheaf.exists_germ_eq p
  obtain ⟨W₂, hxW₂, n₂, hn₂⟩ := F.presheaf.exists_germ_eq q
  have hxW : x ∈ W₁ ⊓ W₂ := ⟨hxW₁, hxW₂⟩
  set d := (denominatorIdealModules X L s).presheaf.map
    (homOfLE (inf_le_left : W₁ ⊓ W₂ ≤ W₁)).op d₁ with hdd
  set n := F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_right : W₁ ⊓ W₂ ≤ W₂)).op n₂ with hnn
  have hpd : grpGerm X.toRingedSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s).val x
      (W₁ ⊓ W₂) hxW d = p :=
    ((denominatorIdealModules X L s).presheaf.germ_res_apply _ x hxW d₁).trans hd₁
  have hqn : grpGerm X.toRingedSpace F.val x (W₁ ⊓ W₂) hxW n = q :=
    (F.presheaf.germ_res_apply _ x hxW n₂).trans hn₂
  have hiso := (tensorStalkIso_germ X.toRingedSpace x
      (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s) F (W₁ ⊓ W₂) hxW d n).trans
    (by rw [hpd, hqn])
  have hsymm : (tensorStalkIso X.toRingedSpace x
        (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s) F).symm (p ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.stalk x] q) =
      (Stacks.Chow.denominatorIdealTensorModule L F s).presheaf.germ (W₁ ⊓ W₂) x hxW
        (toTensorSheafSection X.toRingedSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s) F
          (op (W₁ ⊓ W₂)) (d ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.obj (op (W₁ ⊓ W₂))] n)) :=
    (LinearEquiv.symm_apply_eq _).2 hiso.symm
  have key := (congrArg (fun w => denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x w) hsymm).trans
    (stalkLinearMap_denominatorIdealAction_germ_tmul X L F s x (W₁ ⊓ W₂) hxW d n)
  rw [key]
  exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul
    (Ideal.subset_span ⟨W₁ ⊓ W₂, hxW, _, ⟨d, rfl⟩, rfl⟩) Submodule.mem_top

/-- A germ of the ideal of denominators carries the stalk of `F` into the range of the stalk of
the action: the germ and the element of the stalk are represented on a common neighbourhood and
recombined into a single local pure tensor there. -/
private theorem smul_mem_range_denominatorIdealActionStalk (x : X) {z : X.presheaf.stalk x}
    (hz : z ∈ germs X L s x) (m : F.presheaf.stalk x) :
    z • m ∈ LinearMap.range (denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x) := by
  obtain ⟨W₁, hxW₁, g, ⟨d₁, rfl⟩, rfl⟩ := hz
  obtain ⟨W₂, hxW₂, n₂, hn₂⟩ := F.presheaf.exists_germ_eq m
  have hxW : x ∈ W₁ ⊓ W₂ := ⟨hxW₁, hxW₂⟩
  set d := (denominatorIdealModules X L s).presheaf.map
    (homOfLE (inf_le_left : W₁ ⊓ W₂ ≤ W₁)).op d₁ with hdd
  set n := F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_right : W₁ ⊓ W₂ ≤ W₂)).op n₂ with hnn
  have hqn : F.presheaf.germ (W₁ ⊓ W₂) x hxW n = m :=
    (F.presheaf.germ_res_apply _ x hxW n₂).trans hn₂
  have hres : ((AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op (W₁ ⊓ W₂))).hom d =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left : W₁ ⊓ W₂ ≤ W₁)).op
        (((AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op W₁)).hom d₁) :=
    PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealι X L s).val
      (homOfLE (inf_le_left : W₁ ⊓ W₂ ≤ W₁)).op d₁
  have hgz : X.presheaf.germ (W₁ ⊓ W₂) x hxW
      (((AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op (W₁ ⊓ W₂))).hom d) =
      X.presheaf.germ W₁ x hxW₁
        (((AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op W₁)).hom d₁) := by
    rw [hres]
    exact X.presheaf.germ_res_apply _ x hxW _
  refine ⟨(Stacks.Chow.denominatorIdealTensorModule L F s).presheaf.germ (W₁ ⊓ W₂) x hxW
    (toTensorSheafSection X.toRingedSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s) F
      (op (W₁ ⊓ W₂)) (d ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.obj (op (W₁ ⊓ W₂))] n)), ?_⟩
  rw [stalkLinearMap_denominatorIdealAction_germ_tmul X L F s x (W₁ ⊓ W₂) hxW d n, hgz, hqn]
  rfl

/-- **The range of the stalk of the action of the ideal of denominators is the ideal generated by
the germs of that ideal, acting on the stalk of `F`.** -/
theorem range_denominatorIdealActionStalk (x : X) :
    LinearMap.range (denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x) =
      Ideal.span (germs X L s x) •
        (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) (F.presheaf.stalk x)) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rintro z ⟨w, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ : ∃ t, (tensorStalkIso X.toRingedSpace x
        (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s) F).symm t = w :=
      ⟨tensorStalkIso X.toRingedSpace x (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s) F w,
        LinearEquiv.symm_apply_apply _ _⟩
    induction t using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
    | add a b ha hb =>
        have h2 : denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x
            ((tensorStalkIso X.toRingedSpace x
                (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s) F).symm (a + b)) =
            denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x
              ((tensorStalkIso X.toRingedSpace x
                (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s) F).symm a) +
              denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x
                ((tensorStalkIso X.toRingedSpace x
                  (AlgebraicGeometry.denominatorIdeal X L s) F).symm b) := by
          rw [map_add]
          exact (denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x).map_add _ _
        rw [h2]
        exact Submodule.add_mem _ ha hb
    | tmul p q => exact mem_span_germs_smul_of_tensorStalkIso_symm_tmul X L F s x p q
  · refine Submodule.smul_le.2 fun r hr m _ => ?_
    induction hr using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem z hz => exact smul_mem_range_denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x hz m
    | zero => rw [zero_smul]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _
    | add a b _ _ ha hb => rw [add_smul]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ ha hb
    | smul c a _ ha => rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_smul]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c ha

/-- **The range of the stalk of the action of the ideal of denominators is the denominator ideal
of the germs of a local ratio, acting on the stalk of `F`.** The hypothesis is the colon-ideal
presentation of the ideal of denominators on every basic open of an affine open `V`, exactly as
for `Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk.span_germs_eq_denominatorIdeal`. -/
theorem range_denominatorIdealActionStalk_eq_denominatorIdeal_smul {V : Opens X}
    (hV : IsAffineOpen V) {a b : Γ(X, V)}
    (hbas : ∀ f : Γ(X, V),
      Set.range (ConcreteCategory.hom
          ((Stacks.DenominatorIdeal.denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op (X.basicOpen f)))) =
        {g : Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) | ∃ v : Γ(X, X.basicOpen f),
          g * algebraMap Γ(X, V) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) a =
            algebraMap Γ(X, V) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) b * v})
    {x : X} (hx : x ∈ V) :
    LinearMap.range (denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x) =
      Ideal.denominatorIdeal (X.presheaf.germ V x hx a) (X.presheaf.germ V x hx b) •
        (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) (F.presheaf.stalk x)) := by
  rw [range_denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x,
    span_germs_eq_denominatorIdeal X L s hV hbas hx]

/-- **Around every point of a scheme there is an affine open on which the meromorphic section is a
ratio `a / b` whose denominator ideal, acting on the stalk of `F`, is the range of the stalk of
the action of the ideal of denominators.** The affine open and the ratio come from
`Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk.exists_affineOpen_span_germs_eq_denominatorIdeal`; the only
hypothesis is that `L` is invertible. -/
theorem exists_affineOpen_range_denominatorIdealActionStalk_eq
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.property L)
    (x : X) :
    ∃ (V : Opens X) (hxV : x ∈ V), IsAffineOpen V ∧ ∃ a b : Γ(X, V),
      LinearMap.range (denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x) =
        Ideal.denominatorIdeal (X.presheaf.germ V x hxV a) (X.presheaf.germ V x hxV b) •
          (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) (F.presheaf.stalk x)) := by
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, hVaff, a, b, hspan⟩ :=
    exists_affineOpen_span_germs_eq_denominatorIdeal X L s hL x
  exact ⟨V, hxV, hVaff, a, b, by rw [range_denominatorIdealActionStalk X L F s x, hspan]⟩

/-- **The stalk of the first denominator quotient of [Stacks, Tag 02SW] is the quotient of the
stalk of `F` by the denominator ideal of the germs of a local ratio.** This is
`Stacks.Chow.denominatorQuotientStalkLinearEquiv` with the submodule divided out rewritten by
`Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk.range_denominatorIdealActionStalk_eq_denominatorIdeal_smul`, so that
it is presented by `Ideal.denominatorIdeal`, which is the form the length formula of
[Stacks, Tag 02QH] is stated in. -/
def denominatorQuotientStalkLinearEquivDenominatorIdeal {V : Opens X}
    (hV : IsAffineOpen V) {a b : Γ(X, V)}
    (hbas : ∀ f : Γ(X, V),
      Set.range (ConcreteCategory.hom
          ((Stacks.DenominatorIdeal.denominatorIdealι X L s).val.app (op (X.basicOpen f)))) =
        {g : Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) | ∃ v : Γ(X, X.basicOpen f),
          g * algebraMap Γ(X, V) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) a =
            algebraMap Γ(X, V) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) b * v})
    {x : X} (hx : x ∈ V) :
    (F.presheaf.stalk x ⧸
        (Ideal.denominatorIdeal (X.presheaf.germ V x hx a) (X.presheaf.germ V x hx b) •
          (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) (F.presheaf.stalk x))) : Type u)
      ≃ₗ[X.presheaf.stalk x]
        (Stacks.Chow.denominatorQuotientDecl L F s).presheaf.stalk x :=
  (Submodule.quotEquivOfEq _ _
      (range_denominatorIdealActionStalk_eq_denominatorIdeal_smul X L F s hV hbas hx).symm).trans
    (Stacks.Chow.denominatorQuotientStalkLinearEquiv L F s x)

end Stacks.Chow.DenominatorStalk

end
